      <Desc>Renova, Inc. expands access to mental health care through direct clinical services for California residents. By providing in-person counseling at its clinics in San Diego County, Renova delivers vital support to local patients and families managing mental health conditions. To further increase accessibility, Renova offers need-based sliding scale discounts for therapy sessions conducted by its trainee clinicians, ensuring that financial constraints don't prevent individuals from receiving necessary care. Additionally, its virtual therapy offerings give people throughout California the ability to conveniently access Renova's team of licensed professionals. This combination of affordable in-person and virtual services allows Renova to reach a diverse range of clients with varying needs and financial situations. During the reporting period, Renova served over 300 cases, demonstrating its commitment to improving mental health care access across different communities in California.</Desc>
      <ProgSrvcAccomActy2Grp>
        <ExpenseAmt>277583</ExpenseAmt>
        <GrantAmt>14141</GrantAmt>
        <RevenueAmt>339620</RevenueAmt>
        <Desc>Renova, Inc.'s training program for therapists and doctors improves access to quality mental health care in San Diego County. By providing affordable education in specialized therapies like emotionally focused and play therapy, Renova equips clinicians to offer targeted treatment to community members in need. To enhance accessibility, Renova offers scholarships and discounted rates for 6 of its training courses, ensuring a diverse range of practitioners can benefit from this professional development opportunity. This investment enables practitioners to enhance their skills so they can better serve patients and families managing mental health challenges. During the reporting period, Renova facilitated over 30 training courses overall to mental health clinicians around the world, each spanning 3-6 months. Through these efforts, Renova expands the reach of specialized mental health care and supports the growth of a more skilled and diverse clinical workforce.</Desc>
